+  'elig.cuy.coir': 'The unit you set up must make coir fibre, yarn or coir products. A person, or a group such as a company, self-help group, society, co-operative or trust, can apply.',
+  'elig.cuy.nosub': 'You must not be getting any other government money for the same purpose.',
+  'elig.cuy.edp': 'You must attend a five-day training for new entrepreneurs. It can be before or after you apply, but it must be done before the bank recommends your application.',
+
+  'sdata.sclcss.description': 'Government money for small businesses owned by Scheduled Caste or Scheduled Tribe people that buy machinery with a bank loan. It covers 25% of the loan taken for machinery and equipment, up to Rs.25 lakh. You apply through the bank that gave you the loan.',
+  'sdata.sclcss.support': 'Government money for 25% of the machinery loan',
+  'elig.sclcss.owner': 'The business must be owned by Scheduled Caste or Scheduled Tribe people, who must hold more than 51% of a partnership or company. It must make goods or give services.',
+  'elig.sclcss.loan': 'The money is for machinery or equipment bought with a loan from a bank or another lender. It is not given for machinery that another central or state scheme already supports.',
+
+  'sdata.midh.description': 'Government money for growing and handling fruit, vegetables, flowers, spices, mushrooms, coconut, cashew and bamboo. It helps with nurseries, new orchards and gardens, greenhouses, organic farming, water structures, bee boxes for pollination, machines, and storage and market facilities. Farmers apply through the District or Block Horticulture Officer.',
+  'sdata.midh.support': 'Government money towards the cost of horticulture work',
+  'elig.midh.who': 'Farmers, registered societies and State Governments can take part. A farmer applies through the District or Block Horticulture Officer.',
+  'elig.midh.activities': 'The money is for the crops and kinds of work the mission lists. Rates differ by kind of work and by region.',
+
+  'sdata.acandabc.description': 'Help for agriculture graduates and diploma holders to start their own farm advice centre (Agri-Clinic) or farm services centre (Agri-Business Centre). A clinic advises farmers on soil, crops, plant protection and crop insurance. A centre hires out farm equipment and sells farm inputs. The scheme offers start-up training, a loan and government money towards the cost.',
+  'sdata.acandabc.support': 'Start-up training, a loan and government money towards the cost',
+  'elig.acandabc.age': 'You must be between 18 and 60 years old.',
+  'elig.acandabc.qualification': 'You need a degree in agriculture or a related subject, a diploma in these with at least 50% marks, or an agriculture-related plus-two course with at least 55% marks. A few other farming-related courses are also accepted.',
+  'elig.acandabc.pension': 'A retired employee who receives a pension cannot get the government money under this scheme.',
+
+  'sdata.mszcs.description': 'Government money towards the cost of a ZED quality certificate (Zero Defect Zero Effect). It covers 80% of the cost for a micro unit, 60% for a small unit and 50% for a medium unit, with 10% more for women, Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe owners and for units in the North East, Himalayan areas, islands and aspirational districts.',
+  'sdata.mszcs.support': 'Government money towards the cost of the ZED certificate',
+  'elig.mszcs.unit': 'Your business must be a micro, small or medium enterprise. You register online and take the ZED pledge.',
+
+  'sdata.rkvy_vlstl.description': 'Money to set up a soil testing lab in your village. You get Rs.1.5 lakh, once, paid into your bank account, for the soil testing machine, chemicals and other equipment. It is meant for rural youth, village entrepreneurs, self-help groups, agriculture graduates and farmer co-operatives.',
+  'sdata.rkvy_vlstl.support': 'One-time money of Rs.1.5 lakh',
+  'elig.rkvyvlstl.age': 'You must be 18 to 27 years old and have passed Class 10 with science. Some knowledge of computers is needed.',
+  'elig.rkvyvlstl.premises': 'You or your group must have your own premises, or a rented building with a lease agreement for at least four years.',
+
+  'sdata.smam.description': 'Help to buy farm machines, or to start a centre that hires machines out to farmers. Government money covers 40% or 50% of the cost of a machine you buy, and 40% of the cost of a hiring centre costing up to Rs.250 lakh.',
+  'sdata.smam.support': 'Government money for 40% to 50% of the machine cost',
+  'elig.smam.farmers': 'Government money covers 50% of the machine\'s cost for small and marginal farmers, Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe farmers, women farmers and farmers of the North East and Himalayan states, and 40% for all other farmers. Each machine has its own upper limit.',
+  'elig.smam.chc': 'A rural entrepreneur, self-help group, farmer producer organisation, panchayat or farmers\' co-operative society can set up a hiring centre, with government money for 40% of the project cost for projects costing up to Rs.250 lakh.',
+  'elig.smam.plan': 'Each state decides in its own yearly plan which machines are supported and how many farmers are helped. If there are more applications than the target, they are picked by an online lottery.',
+
+  // --- added 31 Oct 2026, Rajasthan state schemes ---
+  'sdata.rj_digital.description': 'Under its MSME Policy 2024, Rajasthan pays back 75% of what a small business spends on software or equipment to go digital, such as billing machines or stock software. This can be claimed one time, up to Rs.50,000. It also pays back 75% of the fee of one online selling platform, up to Rs.50,000, not counting delivery charges.',
