+  'elig.rjdigital.once': 'You can claim each part only once, and only one online selling platform is covered.',
+
+  'sdata.rj_imsupy.description': 'A scheme of Rajasthan to help women start or grow their own business. An individual woman can get a loan of up to Rs.50 lakh, and a women\'s self-help group up to Rs.1 crore. The scheme provides margin money of 25% of the loan. Loans up to Rs.10 lakh need nothing to pledge as security.',
+  'sdata.rj_imsupy.support': 'Loan of up to Rs.50 lakh for a woman, with margin money of 25%',
+  'elig.rjimsupy.resident': 'You must be a permanent resident of Rajasthan.',
+  'elig.rjimsupy.group': 'A women\'s self-help group, or a cluster or federation of such groups, must be registered with a state government department. A cluster or federation must also be registered under the Cooperative Act.',
+  'elig.rjimsupy.family': 'No one in your family (husband, wife or minor children) should have got help from another central or state scheme for jobs or grants in the last 5 years, and no one in your family should be a defaulter of a bank or other lender.',
+  'elig.rjimsupy.margin': 'Margin money is 25% of the loan, or 30% for women from the Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes, widows, abandoned women, victims of violence and women with a disability. It can be at most Rs.15 lakh.',
+  'elig.rjimsupy.limits': 'The price of land is not counted in the project cost. A loan for building a workshop or other building can be at most 20% of the project amount, and a loan for buying and selling goods can be at most Rs.10 lakh.',
+  'elig.rjimsupy.activities': 'The scheme does not cover making or selling meat products, liquor or other intoxicants, explosives, a transport vehicle with an on-road price above Rs.10 lakh, plastic that cannot be recycled, or anything banned by the government.',
+
+  'sdata.rj_mlupy.description': 'Rajasthan pays part of the interest for up to 5 years on a loan to start or grow a business that makes goods, gives a service or trades. Loans up to Rs.10 crore are covered (Rs.1 crore for trading). The help is 8% on a loan up to Rs.25 lakh, 6% over Rs.25 lakh up to Rs.5 crore, and 5% over Rs.5 crore up to Rs.10 crore.',
+  'sdata.rj_mlupy.support': 'Part of the interest paid by government, 5% to 8%, for up to 5 years',
+  'elig.rjmlupy.who': 'Individuals can apply, and so can groups and organisations such as self-help groups, societies, partnership firms, LLP firms and companies. The business must be set up in Rajasthan, and a person applying must be at least 18 years old.',
+  'elig.rjmlupy.cards': 'People with a Weaver Card can get all of the interest paid back on loans up to Rs.1 lakh. People with a Handicraft or Artisan Card can get the same on loans up to Rs.3 lakh.',
+  'elig.rjmlupy.activities': 'The scheme does not cover making or selling meat, liquor or explosives, plastic that cannot be recycled, or anything banned by the government. It also does not cover a transport vehicle priced above Rs.10 lakh, farming and related work (animals, poultry, fisheries), mining, real estate, schools and coaching, or NGOs and trusts.',
+
+  'sdata.rj_market.description': 'Under its MSME Policy 2024, Rajasthan pays back 75% of the stall rent at a fair or exhibition, or a fixed amount, whichever is smaller: Rs.37,500 in Rajasthan (up to 3 fairs in a financial year), Rs.1,12,500 elsewhere in India (up to 2 fairs), and Rs.1,50,000 abroad (1 fair).',
+  'sdata.rj_market.support': 'Up to 75% of the stall rent paid back at fairs and exhibitions',
+  'elig.rjmarket.fair': 'The fair or exhibition must be sponsored or approved by the government or a government body, or approved by an Export Promotion Council.',
+  'elig.rjmarket.select': 'The Department of Industries and Commerce picks the units by the kind of product they make and the theme of the fair, and prefers units that have not used the scheme before.',
+  'elig.rjmarket.repeat': 'A unit that has used the scheme for one kind of fair (in Rajasthan, elsewhere in India or abroad) cannot use it again for that kind of fair for the next 2 financial years. You must apply within 6 months of the fair or exhibition.',
+
+  'sdata.rj_beekeeping.description': 'Rajasthan\'s Horticulture Department helps farmers and bee-keepers take up bee-keeping. Government money covers 40% of the cost of a bee colony or bee-keeping box, or Rs.800 for each, whichever is lower, for up to 50 colonies and 50 boxes for each person. It is paid straight into the bank account after checks.',
+  'sdata.rj_beekeeping.support': 'Government pays 40% of the cost, up to Rs.800 for each colony or box',
+  'elig.rjbee.farmer': 'You must be a farmer. Preference is given to small and marginal farmers, Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe farmers, women farmers and trained bee-keepers.',
+  'elig.rjbee.apply': 'You apply online at the nearest e-Mitra centre, or through your own e-Mitra account, and applying is free.',
+
+  // --- added 31 Oct 2026, Uttarakhand state schemes ---
+  'sdata.uk_nano.description': 'Bank loans of up to Rs.50,000 to start a very small business or grow one you already have, with government money paid on top. The government money is 25% to 40% and at most Rs.20,000, depending on your district and your category.',
+  'sdata.uk_nano.support': 'Bank loan up to Rs.50,000, with 25% to 40% government money',
+  'elig.uk.nativeResident': 'You must be an original or permanent resident of Uttarakhand.',
+  'elig.uk.noEducation': 'You do not need any school or college qualification.',
+  'elig.uk.bankDefault': 'You must have an account with the bank that gives the loan in your area. You or your business must not have failed to repay a loan to any bank, lender or cooperative bank.',
+  'elig.uknano.subsidy': 'In Category A districts the government money is 35% (up to Rs.17,500) for the general category and 40% (up to Rs.20,000) for the special category. In Category B and B+ districts it is 30% (up to Rs.15,000) and 35% (up to Rs.17,500). In Category C and D districts it is 25% (up to Rs.12,500) and 30% (up to Rs.15,000).',
+  'elig.uknano.release': 'The government money is paid only after your business has run well for one full year without a break.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_msy.description': 'Bank loans for a new factory, service or shop, or for improving a small unit you already have, with government money paid on top. The project can cost up to Rs.25 lakh for making goods and up to Rs.10 lakh for a service or shop. The government money is 15% to 25% depending on your district, and at most Rs.6.25 lakh.',
+  'sdata.uk_msy.support': 'Bank loan with 15% to 25% government money',
+  'elig.ukmsy.sectors': 'Loans are available for factory, service and shop projects, and also for growing apples or orchids, keeping animals and farming.',
+  'elig.ukmsy.release': 'The government money is paid only after your business has run well for two full years without a break.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_tourism.description': 'Bank loans with government money for unemployed people of Uttarakhand to start a tourism business or buy a bus or taxi. For a business, the government money is up to 33% of the cost, at most Rs.33 lakh, in hilly areas, and up to 25%, at most Rs.25 lakh, in plain areas. For a vehicle it is up to 25%, at most Rs.10 lakh.',
+  'sdata.uk_tourism.support': 'Up to 33% government money, at most Rs.33 lakh in hilly areas',
+  'elig.uktour.unemployed': 'You must be unemployed, which means you are not running any business or working in any profession at present.',
+  'elig.uktour.margin': 'To get the government money, you must put in 12.5% of the total project cost yourself, as margin money.',
+  'elig.uktour.land': 'If you need land, you must own it. Land in the name of a close relative also works, if it is pledged to the bank as the first security. Leased land is allowed if the lease is longer than the time you take to repay the loan, and you have not failed to repay any bank or lender.',
+
+  'sdata.uk_minority.description': 'Government money for unemployed people of minority communities in Uttarakhand who take a bank loan of Rs.1 lakh to Rs.10 lakh to start their own work. You get 25% of the loan, at least Rs.25,000 and at most Rs.2,50,000. The bank charges its usual interest on the loan.',
+  'sdata.uk_minority.support': '25% of the loan as government money, Rs.25,000 to Rs.2,50,000',
+  'elig.ukminority.community': 'You must be a permanent resident of Uttarakhand and belong to a minority community: Muslim, Sikh, Christian, Parsi, Buddhist or Jain.',
